  "rulings": [
    {
      "oracle_id": "b3de29cb-7d7d-4566-b5bf-37e571bd5d78",
      "published_at": "2024-09-20",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Dog and Glimmer are both creature types. Enduring Courage won't have those creature types when its last ability returns it to the battlefield because it won't be a creature."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b3de29cb-7d7d-4566-b5bf-37e571bd5d78",
      "published_at": "2024-09-20",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a nontoken permanent that's a copy of Enduring Courage dies while it's a creature, it will return to the battlefield as an enchantment when its last ability resolves. It won't have any card types other than enchantment."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b3de29cb-7d7d-4566-b5bf-37e571bd5d78",
      "published_at": "2024-09-20",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "A token that's a copy of Enduring Courage won't return to the battlefield when its last ability resolves."
    },
    {
      "comment": "Creatures don't necessarily have to be dealt lethal damage by Anger of the Gods to be exiled. After being dealt damage, if they would die for any reason that turn, they'll be exiled instead.",
      "oracle_id": "3a7fe095-8278-4b1d-bec4-19b35bdcdd1b",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura’s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn’t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent’s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura’s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can’t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it’s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Magma Spray's replacement effect will exile the target creature if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage. It applies to the target creature even if Magma Spray deals no damage to it (due to a prevention effect) or Magma Spray deals damage to a different creature (due to a redirection effect).",
      "oracle_id": "fe16f1ab-58b4-4452-abe4-cbd9addd348f",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature dealt damage by Pillar of Flame that dies this turn will be exiled even if it wasn’t the target of Pillar of Flame (because the damage was redirected somehow). If the target creature isn’t dealt damage (most likely because the damage was prevented), it won’t be exiled if it dies that turn.",
      "oracle_id": "468cfc88-a493-44dc-9d0a-63d9cc89c114",
      "published_at": "2017-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature dealt damage by Pillar of Flame will be exiled no matter why the creature would die that turn. It could have its toughness reduced to 0 or less or be destroyed by another spell or ability.",
      "oracle_id": "468cfc88-a493-44dc-9d0a-63d9cc89c114",
      "published_at": "2017-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can target a creature that doesn't have indestructible with Smite the Deathless. It will still be exiled if it would die this turn.",
      "oracle_id": "37994591-3494-4314-a7da-49c112b0866f",
      "published_at": "2023-06-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The damaged creature will be exiled if it would die for any reason that turn, not just if it dies due to damage from Smite the Deathless.",
      "oracle_id": "37994591-3494-4314-a7da-49c112b0866f",
      "published_at": "2023-06-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Smite the Deathless doesn't deal damage to the target creature (perhaps because that damage was prevented), the additional effects will still apply. It will still lose indestructible, and it will be exiled instead of dying that turn.",
      "oracle_id": "37994591-3494-4314-a7da-49c112b0866f",
      "published_at": "2023-06-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Betrayer's Bargain resolves, its effect causes the creature to be exiled any time it would die that turn, not just if it would die as a result of damage dealt by Betrayer's Bargain.",
      "oracle_id": "bfb3d862-d92d-4a4f-9a22-671b55d954fd",
      "published_at": "2024-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Excess damage has been dealt to a creature if the damage dealt to it is greater than lethal damage. Usually, this means damage greater than its toughness, although damage already marked on the creature is taken into account.",
      "oracle_id": "7dc7d90d-5979-4c4a-9183-392e0e0b878a",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In some unusual cases, Hell to Pay may have deathtouch. Even 1 damage dealt to a creature from a source with deathtouch is considered lethal damage, so any amount greater than that will cause excess damage to be dealt, even if the total amount of damage isn’t greater than the creature’s toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "7dc7d90d-5979-4c4a-9183-392e0e0b878a",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
